This package is a modified fork of dsh-screenshot.

  Upstream: https://github.com/paicat1/dsh-screenshot
  Upstream version used: 1.2.0
  Upstream license: MIT (see LICENSE, Copyright (c) 2026 paicat1)

Modifications (2026-10-29):

  dsh/index.js
    - Screen bounds limited to the primary monitor (upstream captured the
      whole virtual desktop, which spans every display).
    - DPI awareness upgraded to Per-Monitor V2, with fallbacks to
      Per-Monitor and System DPI awareness (upstream used System DPI only,
      which made the overlay render stretched on a 125% secondary display).
    - Form.AutoScaleMode set to None so overlay children are positioned in
      exact physical pixels (upstream let WinForms scale them).
    - Region selection waits for an explicit confirm: dragging, clicking a
      window, and clicking the empty desktop all hold the frozen frame and
      show 确定 / 取消 buttons. Upstream captured immediately on mouse-up.
    - Confirm buttons are shown 320 ms after release and ignore clicks that
      are part of the release gesture.
    - Window-snap hover highlight is suppressed while a selection exists, so
      the frozen frame cannot change after release.
    - Dim overlay opacity tuned to 135/255 to match WeChat's screenshot veil.

  dsh/client.js
    - Two on-screen buttons (instant full-screen capture, region selection);
      upstream exposed hotkeys only.
    - Hotkeys retained: Ctrl+Alt+S (arrange then capture) and
      Ctrl+Shift+Alt+S (instant full screen).

No other files were modified. The upstream copyright notice and the full
MIT license text are preserved in LICENSE.
